  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nIssued 344 AM MDT MON OCT 12 2026\nof high pressure will continue to build into the western CONUS, \nkeeping our area in a warm and dry trend Thursday through the \nweekend. Temperatures 5 to 10 degrees above normal remain likely\nFriday through Sunday. Mostly clear skies will be expected \nthroughout the long-term, with some overnight/morning fog \npossible each day. Late Friday through early Saturday, a Pacific\nlongwave trough will dig into the northwest coast and keep our \narea under a dry southwest flow. This flow will continue dry \nconditions and above normal temperatures over the weekend. Come \nMonday, a large upper low will slowly dive down from lower \nBritish Columbia but keep our area under a strong southwest \nflow. This pattern will likely continuing slightly above normal \ntemperatures on Monday. There is long-term guidance on \nwidespread precip associated with this low arriving by late \nMonday, but its timing and magnitude remain slightly uncertain \nfor now.",
